Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 06:24:53 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] 031 (TKFillet): the piece of the sharp edge is a G1 pivot
 border of the corner

Round 2 of the flanked-edge corner (fecbbeeb). The piece of the sharp edge
between the two fillet ends was a free G0 border of the GeomPlate corner, so
the plate met the faces there at whatever angle came out, and at each vertex
of the corner a G0 border met a G1 border. GeomPlate drops the constraint
point of the curve with the lower index at every such vertex (the "point on
curve i is removed" rule of GeomPlate_BuildPlateSurface::Intersect), so which
border kept its end depended on the direction the corner was walked: a
symmetric corner came out asymmetric (owner's part: wall border 15.7 deg at
one end only, sharp-edge creases 29 vs 41 deg), and the edge-piece creases sat
near the offset's tangency threshold (issue 5829 model: PartDesign Thickness
failed, "BRep_API: command not done").

Now the piece is a G1 border on a ruled "pivot" surface through the edge whose
tangent plane turns about the edge from the face of the set-back fillet's line
(far end) to the face the nearer fillet rolls on (near end): the tangent planes
of the rolling ball pivoting on the edge (Rossignac-Requicha). Every vertex of
the corner then joins two G1 borders that agree, so the plate no longer depends
on the border order.

Owner's part (26.3 + HD): symmetric corner, edge tol 6.4e-2 (stock) -> 2.0e-3,
G1 to the fillets 2.0 deg, wall borders <= 2.9 deg, sharp-edge creases
0.9 -> 42.2 deg monotone on both sides, no folds. TestPartDesignApp 226 and
TestPartApp 299 as stock (testCase5829ThicknessOnRotatedFillet passes again).
Only flanked-edge fillet corners change; chamfers and all other corners are
untouched (DRAW blend group logs identical, own sweep with downstream checks).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
